caro: FYI I opened PR #4781 to slim down the quickstart for first-time users. Goals: pick one env var, add a minimal serverless (no-container) first-deploy example, update Node+Python snippets to the new client shape, and fix two broken links. Pls skim.

mike: nice. which env var did you pick? we've got REDWOOD_KEY and API_TOKEN floating in old content.

caro: canonical is REDWOOD_API_KEY. added a one-line migration note for LEGACY_TOKEN and a tiny CI mapping example.

jin: paste the Node example? want to check return shape and close behavior.

caro: Node snippet from the PR:```
const { Redwood } = require('@redwood/inference');
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
const out = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-1', prompt: 'hello quickstart' });
console.log(out.output.text); // output has text + tokens + meta
await client.close();
```

mike: looks good. note to call out Node >=18 and add a comment on loading .env in dev. also prefer `out.output.text` not `out.text`.

jin: on the serverless flow  can you paste that? some workshops avoid Docker so this helps.

caro: added a tiny serverless example for Vercel/Lambda style deploy:```
// api/hello.js (Vercel)
const { Redwood } = require('@redwood/inference');
module.exports = async (req, res) => {
  const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY });
  const out = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood-1', prompt: 'hello from serverless' });
  await client.close();
  res.status(200).send(out.output.text);
};
```

mike: nice. add a brief note about cold-starts and where to put the API key in serverless env vars. Also include a one-liner for local testing: `env REDWOOD_API_KEY=xxx vercel dev`.

jin: paste the Python snippet too?

caro: Python snippet:```python
from redwood import Client
import os
client = Client(api_key=os.getenv('REDWOOD_API_KEY'))
resp = client.generate(model='redwood-1', prompt='hello')
print(resp.output.text)
client.close()
```

jin: add a comment to check `resp.error` in real apps and mention Python >=3.10. Also agree keep streaming out of the main quickstart; add as advanced appendix.

qa-bot: quick lint: PR #4781 missing README anchor update for "deploy options" and one link to private-deploy was 404. Filed as comment.

caro: thanks, fixed the anchor and replaced the broken link with the stable private deploy doc. Added a tiny troubleshooting box: 401 -> check REDWOOD_API_KEY and org allowlist; 429 -> check quota.

mike: two tiny nits: 1) show `await client.close()` in all examples to avoid leaked handles in CI, 2) include a short sentence about ephemeral tokens and link to token rotation guide.

caro: will update both. planning to merge once jin and mike give thumbs so we have the slim quickstart for tomorrow's onboarding run.

docs-bot: PR #4781 labeled docs/quickstart and assigned to caro. Preview build queued.

caro: thanks all, ETA merge in ~45m after minor fixes. If anyone wants to demo the serverless flow in the lab, ping me here. :rocket:
